@meta
id: 07-18
title: Four edits in a deeply nested config
chapter: 07
type: lesson
skills: match-percent, goto-line, zz-center
par: 108
minutes: 12
vscode: fold, unfold, scroll, count the closing braces, get one wrong
open: payment.config.ts

@brief
A 123 line config, nested seven levels deep in places, with runs of four and
five closing braces where the blocks end. Four changes, and every one of
them is about landing on the right bracket rather than about typing.

  1. Line 82 opens the report recipients list. Add `'ops@acme.dev',` as a
     new last entry of that list, after the addresses already there.

  2. Line 20 is the production timeouts, written on one line. It needs a
     third value, so that it reads
     `timeouts: { connect: 2000, read: 5000, total: 10000 },`.

  3. Line 11 opens the key rotation block. Directly after that block closes,
     and at the same level as it, add `lastRotatedAt: '2026-06-01',`. It is
     a sibling of `rotation`, not a member of it, so it goes after the brace
     that closes rotation and before the one that closes credentials.

  4. The `registerPaymentProvider` call that starts on line 3 is not
     terminated. Put a semicolon after the bracket that closes it.

The line numbers above are the ones you are given. Two of these edits add a
line to the file, so the order you work in decides whether the rest of the
numbers are still true when you get to them.

@keys
| `%` | jump to the matching bracket |
| `82G` | line 82 |
| `zz` | put the cursor line in the middle of the screen |
| `o` `O` | open a line below, above |
| `i` `A` | insert before the cursor, append at end of line |
| `h` `k` | left one character, up a line |

@hints
Work from the bottom of the file upwards. Two of the four edits push every
line below them down by one, and the numbers you were given were taken
before any of them happened.
--
You never need to press `f` first. From anywhere on a line, `%` takes the
first bracket at or after the cursor, so `82G` `%` goes from `recipients: [`
to the `]` that closes it, and `20G` `%` goes from the opening brace on that
line to the closing brace on the same line.
--
For the list, `%` lands you on the `]`, so `k` puts you on the last entry
and `o` adds one below it at the right indent. For the rotation block, `%`
lands you on the brace that closes it, and `o` there opens a line that is
already at the level you want. For the timeouts, `%` lands you on the `}`, and
there is a space in front of it, so step back one with `h` before you
insert or you will write your value on the wrong side of the space.

@solution
    82G % k o 'ops@acme.dev', <Esc>
    20G % h i , total: 10000 <Esc>
    11G zz % o lastRotatedAt: '2026-06-01', <Esc>
    3G % A ; <Esc>
    :wq<Enter>

Around ninety keystrokes for four edits in a file nobody could safely count
braces in.

The whole chapter is in this one. `nG` because a number was handed to you,
`%` because a bracket was handed to you, `zz` because you wanted to see the
block you had landed in, `o` and `i` because you already know where the text
goes once you are standing in the right place.

Edit three is the one that separates people who trust `%` from people who
do not. The rotation block ends with `},` and is followed by two more
closing braces in the next two lines. Counting them by eye works here, on a
file you have just read, in a config you wrote. It stops working on a file
you have never seen with a run of five closers, and the failure is silent:
you add your key to the wrong object and the config still parses.

Edit four is the smallest and travels the furthest. Line 3 to line 68 is
sixty-five lines through four levels of nesting, and `%` did it without you
knowing the number — which is just as well, since by the time you got there
you had added two lines above it and the number had changed twice.

That is the shape of everything in this chapter. Say what you mean — that
line, that block, that bracket, that sentence — and let the motion work out
the distance. Distance is what changes when somebody else edits the file.

@start payment.config.ts
import { registerPaymentProvider, defineConfig } from './framework';

registerPaymentProvider({
  name: 'acme-payments',
  environments: {
    production: {
      baseUrl: 'https://api.acme-payments.com/v2',
      credentials: {
        keyId: process.env.ACME_KEY_ID,
        secret: process.env.ACME_SECRET,
        rotation: {
          enabled: true,
          everyDays: 90,
          notify: [
            'payments@acme.dev',
            'security@acme.dev',
          ],
        },
      },
      timeouts: { connect: 2000, read: 5000 },
      retries: {
        attempts: 3,
        backoff: {
          strategy: 'exponential',
          initialMs: 250,
          maxMs: 8000,
        },
        retryOn: [502, 503, 504],
      },
    },
    sandbox: {
      baseUrl: 'https://sandbox.acme-payments.com/v2',
      credentials: {
        keyId: process.env.ACME_SANDBOX_KEY_ID,
        secret: process.env.ACME_SANDBOX_SECRET,
        rotation: {
          enabled: false,
          everyDays: 0,
          notify: [],
        },
      },
      timeouts: { connect: 5000, read: 15000 },
      retries: {
        attempts: 1,
        backoff: {
          strategy: 'fixed',
          initialMs: 1000,
          maxMs: 1000,
        },
        retryOn: [503],
      },
    },
  },
  webhooks: {
    endpoint: '/webhooks/acme',
    events: [
      'refund.created',
      'refund.settled',
      'refund.failed',
      'payment.captured',
    ],
    signature: {
      header: 'x-acme-signature',
      algorithm: 'sha256',
      toleranceSeconds: 300,
    },
  },
})

export const reconciliation = defineConfig({
  schedule: {
    cron: '0 5 * * *',
    timezone: 'Europe/London',
  },
  window: {
    days: 7,
    includeUnsettled: true,
  },
  report: {
    name: 'settlement-reconciliation',
    format: 'csv',
    recipients: [
      'finance@acme.dev',
      'payments@acme.dev',
    ],
    columns: [
      'order',
      'reference',
      'amount',
      'settled',
      'discrepancy',
    ],
    delivery: {
      transport: 'email',
      retries: {
        attempts: 2,
        backoff: {
          strategy: 'fixed',
          initialMs: 60000,
          maxMs: 60000,
        },
      },
    },
  },
  alerts: {
    onDiscrepancy: {
      channel: '#payments-alerts',
      mention: ['@payments-oncall'],
      threshold: {
        count: 1,
        amountMinorUnits: 1000,
      },
    },
    onFailure: {
      channel: '#payments-alerts',
      mention: ['@payments-oncall', '@sre-oncall'],
      threshold: {
        count: 1,
        amountMinorUnits: 0,
      },
    },
  },
});

@expected payment.config.ts
import { registerPaymentProvider, defineConfig } from './framework';

registerPaymentProvider({
  name: 'acme-payments',
  environments: {
    production: {
      baseUrl: 'https://api.acme-payments.com/v2',
      credentials: {
        keyId: process.env.ACME_KEY_ID,
